{"status": "done", "model": "gpt-6-astra", "effort": "high", "n_calls": 13, "api_errors": 2, "started": 1790566585.779796, "usage": {"input": 129555, "output": 3579, "reasoning": 553, "cached": 110848}, "items": [{"role": "developer", "content": "You are an autonomous software/ML engineering agent working in a Linux sandbox (Python 3.10 + numpy; no internet package installs). There is no human available: never ask questions, make reasonable decisions and keep working until the task is fully complete. Use the `shell` tool to inspect files, run experiments and edit code. When you are completely done, reply with a brief final summary and do not call any tool in that final message."}, {"role": "user", "content": "# Choose the data mixture for a data-constrained pre-training run\n\nYou are the data lead for a pre-training run that will be launched exactly once with a fixed shape:\na **2.5B-parameter** (non-embedding) model trained on **500B tokens**. The training corpus has four domains -\n`web`, `code`, `math`, `papers` - each with a fixed, finite amount of unique text (see `/app/docs/corpora.md`).\nYour job: choose the sampling mixture for that run, and forecast its final composite evaluation loss so the\nplanning team can budget follow-up work.\n\nYou cannot run the target. You can run small proxy trainings in a simulated lab. Run `/app/bin/lab spec`\nfirst. Each `train` call trains a fresh model with N parameters on D tokens using your mixture and returns its\nheld-out losses on three eval sets (general, code, math) and their weighted composite. Like real training runs,\nproxy results carry run-to-run noise. Proxy compute is limited: 5e+19 FLOPs in total, a run costs 6*N*D.\nExample:\n\n    /app/bin/lab train N=1e8 D=2e9 --json '{\"mix\": {\"web\": 0.7, \"code\": 0.1, \"math\": 0.1, \"papers\": 0.1}}'\n\n## Deliverable: `/app/mixture.json`\n\n    {\"mixture\": {\"web\": 0.0, \"code\": 0.0, \"math\": 0.0, \"papers\": 0.0},\n     \"predicted_loss\": {\"lo\": 0.0, \"hi\": 0.0}}\n\n* `mixture` - sampling weights (non-negative, sum to 1). The target run draws `mixture[d] * 500B` tokens from\n  domain d; if that is more than the domain's unique tokens, the domain's data is repeated (several epochs).\n* `predicted_loss` - an interval for the target run's final composite eval loss (its expected value, without\n  run-to-run noise) *for the mixture you submit*. Width at most 0.09.\n\n## How it is graded (mechanically, against the simulator; only the file counts)\n\n1. `mixture.json` is valid (weights, interval, width <= 0.09).\n2. The target run's composite loss with your mixture is within **0.0025** of the lowest composite loss any\n   mixture can reach for this target run.\n3. Your interval contains the target run's composite loss with your mixture.\n\nAll three must hold. Your lab history is not graded; spend the budget however you think is best. When you are\ndone, make sure `/app/mixture.json` is written, then stop.\n"}, {"id": "msg_03afdac4846fd2c0016ab9e3b0f35c87d29c99e78903fb0586", "type": "message", "content": [{"type": "output_text", "annotations": [], "logprobs": [], "text": "I\u2019ll inspect the lab specification and corpus limits, then use proxy runs to estimate the best mixture and forecast its target loss.\n"}], "internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough": {"create_time": 1790567344.169538, "turn_id": "01a0e621-6422-798e-9ecc-46be76fda6cc"}, "phase": "commentary", "role": "assistant", "metadata": {"turn_id": "01a0e621-6422-798e-9ecc-46be76fda6cc"}}, {"id": "fc_03afdac4846fd2c0016ab9e3b21bf887d28bbcc1dbf3b337df", "type": "function_call", "arguments": "{\"command\":[\"/app/bin/lab\",\"spec\"],\"timeout_ms\":10000,\"workdir\":\"/app\"}", "call_id": "call_i8H9yzqDQZMOslO7l0gpQa0Y", "internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough": {"create_time": 1790567344.169538, "turn_id": "01a0e621-6422-798e-9ecc-46be76fda6cc"}, "name": "shell", "metadata": {"turn_id": "01a0e621-6422-798e-9ecc-46be76fda6cc"}}, {"type": "function_call_output", "call_id": "call_i8H9yzqDQZMOslO7l0gpQa0Y", "output": "{\"exit_code\": 0, \"duration_s\": 0.0, \"output\": \"{\\n \\\"ops\\\": {\\n  \\\"train\\\": {\\n   \\\"args\\\": {\\n    \\\"N\\\": \\\"non-embedding parameters, 5e+07..4e+08\\\",\\n    \\\"D\\\": \\\"training tokens, 1e+09..2e+10\\\",\\n    \\\"mix\\\": \\\"sampling weights over ['web', 'code', 'math', 'papers'] (sum to 1)\\\",\\n    \\\"pool\\\": \\\"optional {domain: unique tokens}: restrict the unique data a run may draw from (default: the full corpus for every domain); tokens beyond the pool are repeats\\\"\\n   },\\n   \\\"cost\\\": \\\"6*N*D FLOPs\\\",\\n   \\\"returns\\\": \\\"eval_loss per eval set (['general', 'code', 'math']), composite (weighted by {'general': 0.237, 'code': 0.36, 'math': 0.403}), tokens_seen / unique_tokens_available / epochs per domain\\\"\\n  }\\n },\\n \\\"corpus_unique_tokens\\\": {\\n  \\\"web\\\": 3000000000000.0,\\n  \\\"code\\\": 36410989526.00656,\\n  \\\"math\\\": 9967276924.74475,\\n  \\\"papers\\\": 23536988791.987087\\n },\\n \\\"target\\\": {\\n  \\\"N\\\": 2500000000.0,\\n  \\\"D\\\": 500000000000.0\\n },\\n \\\"deliverable\\\": \\\"/app/mixture.json\\\",\\n \\\"budget_total\\\": 5e+19,\\n \\\"budget_left\\\": 5e+19\\n}\\n\"}"}, {"id": "fc_03afdac4846fd2c0016ab9e3b6d26c87d2b070fa3776012b98", "type": "function_call", "arguments": "{\"command\":[\"bash\",\"-lc\",\"cat /app/docs/corpora.md && ls -la /app && ls -la /app/bin\"],\"timeout_ms\":10000,\"workdir\":\"/app\"}", "call_id": "call_2WOtuAVEW2VeXAF7hHIpvWXc", "internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough": {"create_time": 1790567349.760829, "turn_id": "01a0e621-7922-7f13-942f-adf2d6611355"}, "name": "shell", "metadata": {"turn_id": "01a0e621-7922-7f13-942f-adf2d6611355"}}, {"type": "function_call_output", "call_id": "call_2WOtuAVEW2VeXAF7hHIpvWXc", "output": "{\"exit_code\": 0, \"duration_s\": 0.0, \"output\": \"# Training corpora (unique tokens after dedup)\\n\\n| domain | unique tokens | notes |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| web    | 3.0e+12 | filtered CommonCrawl-style web text; effectively inexhaustible at our scale |\\n| code   | 3.6e+10 | permissively licensed source code, deduplicated at file level |\\n| math   | 1.0e+10 | math web pages, textbooks and worked solutions |\\n| papers | 2.4e+10 | scientific papers (full text) |\\n\\nEval sets (held out, never trained on): `general` (broad web/knowledge text), `code` (code completion),\\n`math` (math problems with solutions).  The team's headline number is the composite\\n`0.237 * general + 0.36 * code + 0.403 * math`.\\n\\nThe target run: 2.5B non-embedding parameters, 500B training tokens, single run, standard recipe\\n(the proxies use the same recipe at smaller size).\\ntotal 16\\ndrwx------  4 dazzling-upbeat-fermat dazzling-upbeat-fermat 4096 Sep 28 03:36 .\\ndrwxr-xr-x 10 dazzling-upbeat-fermat dazzling-upbeat-fermat  260 Sep 28 03:49 ..\\n-rw-r--r--  1 dazzling-upbeat-fermat dazzling-upbeat-fermat   32 Sep 28 03:36 .lab_token\\ndrwx------  2 dazzling-upbeat-fermat dazzling-upbeat-fermat 4096 Sep 28 03:35 bin\\ndrwx------  2 dazzling-upbeat-fermat dazzling-upbeat-fermat 4096 Sep 28 03:35 docs\\ntotal 12\\ndrwx------ 2 dazzling-upbeat-fermat dazzling-upbeat-fermat 4096 Sep 28 03:35 .\\ndrwx------ 4 dazzling-upbeat-fermat dazzling-upbeat-fermat 4096 Sep 28 03:36 ..\\n-rwx------ 1 dazzling-upbeat-fermat dazzling-upbeat-fermat 3226 Sep 28 03:35 lab\\n\"}"}, {"id": "rs_03afdac4846fd2c0016ab9e3bb120087d2ad7abfd28aa6c199", "type": "reasoning", "content": [], "encrypted_content": "gAAAAABqueO8sKIPxfmP0zaW54Sx5jbVsRS-YTnafLbH_J4TX8KABL1KD6DCRr4mt5ZJcy06FTn5MycSFegJQ2rIVJcG8sQH8jjlTrTQVvSBfbjNLsjEMC3rzPW-bp8PlULcPkfkNIWohLqrnp1z59OaA08EiZsrWpP8qZkT8szb9LUm3Kx2bo1Tq2-YkQpn12RUDMV0PGxMLIEbKrgPcUGFfeQFKoVQezzurhmFexLRSYhDLtdIqbuEjzvTj-2iYaCVPqXaFA6Br2xtYuEZMexTQ_WMn0SmY7bk56IW0IygaSoz0EI-5bM5gr07_4g0n8q8SD2qpYiZC3_CuLvjqJKnMNSw3uKGKoraWFuwFpd-os9T8p3rwXqjj3IJUNU-n4pjyfx3rBsM0JP5vLjUOhzPyxyonZwHo4Z0N4OEsisiqhUXKZZDBDYk4xbAaphCqIGWpVfe2Omy3Zk